        "text": "Prince Hamlet of Denmark is visited by his father's ghost, who reveals that Hamlet's uncle Claudius murdered him, seized the throne, and married Hamlet's mother Gertrude—prompting Hamlet to feign madness while seeking proof of the crime and plotting revenge. After confirming Claudius's guilt through a staged play, Hamlet's hesitant quest for vengeance spirals into catastrophe: Polonius is killed, Ophelia goes mad and drowns, and in the final duel, Claudius, Gertrude, Laertes, and Hamlet himself all perish.",
